---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// `/events/christmas-party-2026/` — the club's Christmas party, and its ticket form.
//
// ## What ships in this file, and what the Worker paints
//
// **Every fact about the occasion is painted from `store.socials`.** Not one word about the
// date, the time, the venue, the age limit or the price is written here — they are columns,
// and what ships in this file is the state before any of them was supplied: every row reading
// "To be confirmed", and tickets not on sale.
//
// That is not a hypothetical. All five were supplied on 5 September 2026 and went in as two
// `update`s in two migrations, with this file untouched — which is the property the whole
// arrangement exists for, and the reason a stale date can never be stranded in markup here.
//
// That is the same arrangement `/nn/<year>/` uses and it is chosen for the same reason: **a
// page that cannot reach the database must not offer to take money.** Every failure — an
// unreachable database, a migration that has not landed, a slug that does not exist — leaves
// this markup exactly as it is, which sells nothing and claims nothing.
//
// ## ⚠️ The form ships hidden AND disabled, and both are load-bearing
//
// `hidden` does not stop a control being validated. A `required` input inside a hidden
// container is still constrained, still empty and still invalid, so the browser silently
// refuses to submit the form the control is in — no request, no row, no visible error. That
// took the live entry form down for every signed-in runner on 31 August 2026, and it was found
// by accident. `worker/events.ts` clears both together and never one alone.
//
// ## What is deliberately not asked for
//
// The 2025 party page asked people to state dietary requirements while booking. This form does
// not, and the confirmation email asks for them by reply instead: an allergy is health data and
// a religious diet reveals belief, so both are Article 9 and both would need an explicit
// condition, a retention period, and items on two privacy notices before one could be stored.
// See ADR-033.
---

<Base
  title="SRC Christmas Party 2026 — Southville Running Club"
  description="The Southville Running Club Christmas party. Details to be confirmed."
>
  <h1 data-social-name>SRC Christmas Party 2026</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    One of the big events in the Southville Running Club calendar — our annual Christmas
    party.
  </p>

  {
    /*
      **The club's own poster, and it is the one place on this page a fact is not painted from
      the database.**

      ⚠️ **The date and the venue are baked into the artwork.** Everything else here reads
      `store.socials`, so confirming or changing a fact is an `update` and no deploy — but this
      image cannot be updated that way. If the committee ever moves the party, **the poster
      goes stale silently while the text beside it corrects itself**, which is the worse half:
      a visitor believes the picture. Regenerating it is a step in the runbook for exactly that
      reason, and the generator has a details-free variant for the case where a date is in
      doubt.

      **An `<img>` rather than a CSS background**, which is the opposite of what the two
      campaign pages do — `nn/index.astro` says a decorative image is a background "because it
      is decoration that states nothing". This one states plenty, so it is content.

      **The alt text says what the picture is, not what it says.** The date and the venue are
      in real text directly below, and repeating them here would make a screen reader read the
      party twice; what a non-sighted reader actually gains from this element is knowing there
      is a poster and roughly what is on it.

      `width` and `height` are the intrinsic pixel size, so the browser reserves the right box
      before the file arrives and the facts below do not jump down the page as it loads.
    */
  }
  <img
    src="/src-christmas-party-2026-1080.webp"
    width="1080"
    height="1080"
    alt="The club's Christmas party poster — a running Santa and club runners among snowflakes and Christmas trees."
    class="social-poster"
  />

  {
    /* **The facts, each painted only when the database holds one.** A cell whose column is
      null keeps the words below, which are true. Nothing here falls back to last year. */
  }
  <dl>
    <dt>Date</dt>
    <dd data-social-date>To be confirmed</dd>

    <dt>Time</dt>
    <dd data-social-times>To be confirmed</dd>

    <dt>Where</dt>
    <dd data-social-venue>To be confirmed</dd>

    <dt>Price</dt>
    <dd data-social-price>To be confirmed</dd>
  </dl>

  {
    /* Ships hidden: an age limit is a fact about the occasion and there is not one recorded. */
  }
  <p data-social-age hidden>Entry requirements</p>

  {
    /*
    **It does not name which details are missing, and that is deliberate.** This sentence
    listed the date, the venue and the price — and went stale within a day, when the date and
    the venue were supplied. The rows above each carry their own "To be confirmed", which is
    both more precise and painted from the same columns, so there is exactly one place a
    missing fact is announced from and it cannot disagree with itself.

    Revealed whenever `socialDetailsConfirmed()` is false — the date, the venue *and* the
    start time all present — so it takes itself down when there is nothing left to say.
  */
  }
  <p data-social-unconfirmed>
    <strong>Some details for 2026 are still to be confirmed.</strong> Anything above marked
    "To be confirmed" has not been settled yet, and this page will show it as soon as it is.
    Nothing here is carried over from last year.
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="tickets-heading">
    <h2 id="tickets-heading">Tickets</h2>

    {
      /* **Inside the section it is about, not above it.** It sat above this heading, which
        left "Tickets" reading as an empty section and put the answer before the question.
        This is the default state and the one production serves today; the Worker hides it
        only when the sales window is open *and* a price exists. */
    }
    <p data-social-closed>
      Tickets are not on sale yet. Keep an eye on this page, or ask at a club run.
    </p>

    {/* Ships hidden and every control ships disabled — see this file's header. */}
    <form method="post" action="/events/christmas-party-2026/" data-social-form hidden>
      {
        /*
        **The error summary is the first child of the form, not a block above it.** A
        container's message belongs to that container, and this page could grow a second form.
        Each item links to the field it is about, which is the half that makes it navigable
        rather than merely announced.

        ⚠️ Do not add a CSS `@view-transition` to this page. Four lines of it, with no
        JavaScript at all, made the overlay swallow the click on exactly this kind of link
        after a 422 — silently, so the person just finds that nothing happens. It passes with
        scripting on, which is what makes it easy to ship. The note is at the foot of
        `packages/shared/styles/nn-theme.css`.
      */
      }
      <div
        class="notice notice-bad"
        role="alert"
        data-social-error-summary
        tabindex="-1"
        hidden
      >
        <h3>There is a problem</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#purchaserName" data-social-error="purchaserName" hidden></a></li>
          <li><a href="#email" data-social-error="email" hidden></a></li>
          <li><a href="#emailConfirm" data-social-error="emailConfirm" hidden></a></li>
          <li><a href="#quantity" data-social-error="quantity" hidden></a></li>
          <li><a href="#ticketCode" data-social-error="ticketCode" hidden></a></li>
          <li><span data-social-error="consents" hidden></span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="notice notice-bad" role="alert" data-social-refusal hidden></p>

      <div class="field">
        <label class="field-label" for="purchaserName">Your name</label>
        <p
          class="field-error"
          id="purchaserName-error"
          data-social-error="purchaserName"
          hidden
        >
        </p>
        <input
          class="field-input"
          id="purchaserName"
          name="purchaserName"
          type="text"
          autocomplete="name"
          maxlength="120"
          aria-describedby="purchaserName-error"
          required
          disabled
          data-social-field="purchaserName"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <label class="field-label" for="email">Your email address</label>
        <p class="field-hint" id="email-hint">
          We will send your ticket confirmation here.
        </p>
        <p class="field-error" id="email-error" data-social-error="email" hidden></p>
        <input
          class="field-input"
          id="email"
          name="email"
          type="email"
          autocomplete="email"
          maxlength="254"
          aria-describedby="email-error email-hint"
          required
          disabled
          data-social-field="email"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <label class="field-label" for="emailConfirm">Type your email address again</label
        >
        <p
          class="field-error"
          id="emailConfirm-error"
          data-social-error="emailConfirm"
          hidden
        >
        </p>
        <input
          class="field-input"
          id="emailConfirm"
          name="emailConfirm"
          type="email"
          autocomplete="email"
          maxlength="254"
          aria-describedby="emailConfirm-error"
          required
          disabled
          data-social-field="emailConfirm"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <label class="field-label" for="quantity">How many tickets</label>
        <p class="field-error" id="quantity-error" data-social-error="quantity" hidden>
        </p>
        {
          /*
          **The options ship empty and the Worker fills them**, exactly as the fee cards and
          the previous-years pills do — because the alternative is assembling markup from data
          with `setInnerContent(..., { html: true })`, and there is deliberately no such call
          anywhere in this repository to audit.

          **Twenty of them, because that is `max_tickets_per_purchase`'s own check
          constraint.** Shipping fewer would silently cap an occasion the database would have
          allowed; the Worker removes the ones above whatever this occasion actually permits,
          so the markup and the constraint cannot disagree.

          Each label carries the total for that quantity, built by `quantityOptionLabel` with
          `formatPence` — so the price shown and the price charged multiply the same
          `price_pence`, and it works with scripting off. A client script that writes its own
          `£` is the pattern issue #175 already tracks six instances of.
        */
        }
        <select
          class="field-input"
          id="quantity"
          name="quantity"
          aria-describedby="quantity-error"
          required
          disabled
        >
          {
            Array.from({ length: 20 }, (_unused, index) => (
              <option value={index + 1} data-social-quantity={index + 1} />
            ))
          }
        </select>
      </div>

      {
        /* Which ticket type, painted by the Worker from `store.ticket_types`. Hidden because
          there is one price; it becomes a visible choice the day there is more than one. */
      }
      <input type="hidden" name="ticketCode" value="" disabled data-social-ticket-code />

      <button class="button" type="submit" disabled>Buy tickets</button>

      <p>You will be taken to Stripe to pay. The club never sees your card details.</p>
    </form>
  </section>

  <p>
    {
      /*
      ⚠️ **`{' '}` rather than a line break, and it is not decoration.** Astro follows JSX's
      whitespace rule: whitespace containing a newline, next to an element, is removed. So
      `Email` on one line and `<a>` on the next renders as `Emailinfo@…` — which is what this
      line did until it was looked at in a browser. Prettier will keep reflowing this
      paragraph, so the space has to be a thing in the markup rather than a thing in the
      layout. CLAUDE.md names the same trap one framework along, in `worker/html.ts`.
    */
    }
    Questions about the party? Email{' '}
    <a href="mailto:info@southvillerunningclub.co.uk">info@southvillerunningclub.co.uk</a
    >.
  </p>

  <footer>
    <p>Southville Running Club.</p>
  </footer>
</Base>
